.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt CBLINK-GEN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cblink-gen
.Nd generate C code and documentation from a cblink family spec
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl BnV
.Op Fl b Ar base
.Op Fl m Ar parts
.Op Fl o Ar dir
.Ar spec.yaml
.Nm
.Op Fl adn
.Op Fl F Ar module : Ns Ar feature , Ns ...
.Op Fl b Ar base
.Op Fl m Cm h , Ns Cm md , Ns Cm schema , Ns Cm server , Ns Cm sid , Ns Cm sidjson , Ns Cm tree
.Op Fl o Ar dir
.Op Fl p Ar dir
.Op Fl s Ar file.sid
.Ar module.yang ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads the description of a
.Xr cblink 3
family from
.Ar spec.yaml
and writes the C code that servers and clients of that family use:
typed request and reply structures, policies, parsers, builders,
client wrappers and server registration.
It plays the part YNL plays for Linux netlink.
The spec format, a subset of YAML, is described in
.Pa docs/SPEC-FORMAT.md
in the cblink sources.
.Pp
The output is deterministic: the same spec always gives byte-identical
files, so generated code can be committed and checked.
Files are written atomically: each is created under a temporary name in
.Ar dir
and renamed into place, so an interrupted run leaves the previous files
intact.
.Pp
The spec is untrusted input.
.Nm
opens the spec and the output directory, then enters
.Xr capsicum 4
capability mode before it parses anything.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "-m parts"
.It Fl a
For YANG modules: give a SID to each item of the module of every
.Fl s
file that has none, and rewrite the file.
The items are numbered as RFC 9595 Appendix B says: by namespace
(module, identities, features, data), each in identifier order, every
one the next SID free in the file's assignment ranges.
A file that had items gets the next
.Ql sid-file-version ,
and its
.Ql dependency-revision
becomes the revisions the module's imports are bound to.
Running it again on a complete file changes nothing.
.It Fl B
Allow what is reserved for families built into the library:
the family names
.Ql ctrl
and
.Ql cblink.* ,
and a
.Ql fixed-id .
Only the control family uses this.
.It Fl d
For YANG modules: print the generator's model of the compiled schema,
a schema node a line (its module, kind, path and flags), for comparison
with
.Xr yanglint 1 .
.It Fl F Ar module : Ns Ar feature , Ns ...
For YANG modules: the features of
.Ar module
to enable,
.Ql *
for all of them, none for none.
It may be given up to 64 times.
Without
.Fl F ,
every feature of every implemented module is on; with it, only those
named are, as with
.Xr yanglint 1 .
What a disabled feature guards is left out, identities, enums and bits
included; the deviations of the modules loaded are applied.
.It Fl b Ar base
Name the output files
.Ar base Ns .h ,
.Ar base Ns .c
and so on.
The default is the spec's file name without
.Pa .yaml ;
for YANG modules, the first module's name, without its revision.
.It Fl m Ar parts
A comma-separated list of the files to write:
.Bl -tag -width "server"
.It Cm h
.Ar base Ns .h :
constants, attribute and command enumerations, structures and all
prototypes.
.It Cm c
.Ar base Ns .c :
policies, parsers and builders, needed by both sides.
.It Cm client
.Ar base Ns _client.c :
client wrappers for requests (synchronous, and asynchronous for loop
callbacks), dumps, subscriptions and streams.
.It Cm server
.Ar base Ns _server.c :
the family definition, registration and reply helpers; the server
supplies the handler functions declared in the header.
.It Cm md
.Ar base Ns .md :
reference documentation in Markdown.
.El
.Pp
The default is
.Ql h,c,client,server,md .
For YANG modules these are written yet:
.Bl -tag -width "sidjson"
.It Cm h
.Ar base Ns .h ,
.Ar base
the first module's name by default: a struct for each container, list
entry, rpc and action input and output, notification and structure of
the modules named and of those whose trees they add to, and one for
each module's top-level data.
A container is a pointer, NULL when absent; a list or leaf-list a
count and an array; a scalar leaf other than a key has a
.Ql has_
flag; a choice is an enum saying its case, its cases' members beside
it; a union a struct saying which member is set.
Names are the module's, then the path, with
.Ql -
and
.Ql \&.
made
.Ql _ ;
two nodes that would have one name are an error.
The header declares
.Va base Ns _schema ,
the tables
.Cm schema
writes, and for each struct but a module's data
.Ft int
.Fn struct_encode
and
.Fn struct_decode ,
its value in YANG-CBOR and back, and
.Fn struct_put
and
.Fn struct_parse ,
the same in a message as
.Brq SID : value ,
an rpc's input and output under the rpc's SID; for each rpc
.Fn rpc_call ,
the rpc called through family 1, and for each notification
.Fn notification_notify ,
sent to its subscribers.
.Cm schema
defines them with
.Xr cblink 3 Ns 's
.Fn cbl_yencode ,
.Fn cbl_ydecode ,
.Fn cbl_msg_put_ynode ,
.Fn cbl_msg_ydecode ,
.Fn cbl_request
and
.Fn cbl_ynotify .
.It Cm server
.Ar base Ns _server.c :
a server's handler table, the
.Vt cbl_yserver
.Va base Ns _server
.Xr cblink 3
serves the modules by: for each top-level data node
.Fn node_get
and, a configuration node,
.Fn node_edit ;
for each rpc
.Fn rpc_rpc ,
each action
.Fn action_action ,
which the program defines as the header declares them, the names
those of the nodes' structs; and each notification's
.Fn notification_notification ,
which
.Cm schema
defines, writes it as
.Brq SID : value .
.It Cm schema
.Ar base Ns _schema.c :
the schema tables of the same modules, the structures of
.In cbl_schema.h
the library decodes, encodes and validates YANG-CBOR by: every node
with its SID, its type, its children sorted by SID, its keys, choices,
when and must expressions, defaults and limits; types shared between
the nodes that have the same one, a pattern also as the POSIX ERE it
translates to; each module's features, enabled or not; and the
identities a value may name, the modules' own and every one derived
from a base an identityref has, wherever it is defined, each with all
those derived from it, by SID, for
.Fn derived-from .
A node's children are found by a key's delta at once where their SIDs
follow one another, by a table of their places where they lie close,
by a binary search otherwise; every node is also in one array by SID.
.Xr cblink 3 Ns 's
.Fn cbl_ynode_child ,
.Fn cbl_yschema_node ,
.Fn cbl_yschema_ident
and
.Fn cbl_yderived_from
look them up.
Every node, structure and identityref base must have a SID: the
modules'
.Pa .sid
files are given with
.Fl s .
What each module's tables come to, its trees with what other modules
add to them, is printed and written at the top of the file.
The tables also say where each node is in the structs of
.Cm h :
its member's offset, its
.Ql has_
flag's, its struct's size, written with
.Fn offsetof
and
.Fn sizeof ,
so that the two cannot differ.
.It Cm md
.Ar base Ns .md :
a page of Markdown for each module named: its tree diagram, and a
table of the nodes it defines, in its own tree and in those it
augments, with their kind, type, config, mandatory, defaults, units
and, when its
.Pa .sid
file is attached with
.Fl s ,
their SIDs; then its features and identities.
.It Cm sid
.Ar module Ns @ Ns Ar revision Ns .sid.cbor ,
one for each
.Fl s
file:
the file in YANG-CBOR (RFC 9254), its
.Ql ietf-sid-file
structure keyed by SIDs, as cblink's GET-SID answers it.
.It Cm sidjson
.Ar module Ns @ Ns Ar revision Ns .sid ,
one for each
.Fl s
file:
the file in JSON, as
.Fl a
writes it.
.It Cm tree
.Ar base Ns .tree :
the tree diagrams (RFC 8340) of the modules named, exactly as
.Ql yanglint -f tree
prints them: a module's own tree, rpcs and notifications compiled,
with the nodes other modules augment into them; its augments of other
modules' trees as written, a grouping used there as one
.Ql -u
line; then its structures and yang-data.
Lines are not wrapped.
.El
.It Fl n
Check the spec and report problems without writing anything.
For a YANG module, report what was compiled.
.It Fl p Ar dir
Look for the modules a YANG module imports in
.Ar dir ,
as well as in the module's own directory.
It may be given up to 16 times.
.It Fl s Ar file.sid
For YANG modules: attach the YANG Schema Item iDentifiers of a module
from an RFC 9595
.Pa .sid
file, in JSON or in the YANG-CBOR form
.Fl m Cm sid
writes, and verify them: no SID given twice, none outside the file's
assignment ranges, and every item of the module with one, empty
.Ql input
and
.Ql output
included.
It may be given up to 256 times.
.It Fl o Ar dir
Write the files into
.Ar dir
instead of the current directory.
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Ss YANG modules
A file named
.Ar name Ns .yang
or
.Ar name Ns @ Ns Ar revision Ns .yang
is a YANG module, read through libyang when
.Nm
is built with it
.Pq Va CBLINK_GEN_LIBYANG ,
which it is when libyang 3 is installed.
Every module it may import is read before capability mode is entered,
from its own directory and each
.Fl p
directory; a module imported without a revision is the latest found.
Several may be named.
Only
.Fl n ,
.Fl d
and the parts of
.Fl m
named above are supported yet: the modules are parsed and compiled, and errors are
reported as for a spec.
.Pp
The file
.Pa share/yang/ietf-sid-file@2024-07-31.sid
of cblink's sources holds the SIDs the YANG-CBOR form is keyed by: IANA's range for the
module, 1300 to 1349, numbered as RFC 9595 Appendix B says, IANA having
published no
.Pa .sid
file for it.
A
.Nm
built without libyang refuses YANG modules.
.Ss Building with make
.Pa ${LOCALBASE}/share/cblink/cblink.mk
runs
.Nm
from a
.Xr bsd.prog.mk 5
Makefile:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PROG=		kvd
SRCS=		kvd.c
CBLINK_SPECS=	kv.yaml
\&.include "${LOCALBASE}/share/cblink/cblink.mk"
\&.include <bsd.prog.mk>
.Ed
.Pp
See the comment at the top of
.Pa cblink.mk
for its variables.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "${LOCALBASE}/share/cblink/yang" -compact
.It Pa ${LOCALBASE}/share/cblink/cblink.mk
make rules for programs built from specs and modules
.It Pa ${LOCALBASE}/share/cblink/yang
the YANG modules of cblink's wire version 2, with their
.Pa .sid
files: the framework's structures
.Pq Pa cblink ,
the control family
.Pq Pa cblink-ctrl
and
.Pa ietf-sid-file
for GET-SID
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "0"
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
The spec is invalid; every problem found is reported on standard error as
.Ar file : Ns Ar line : Ns Ar column : Li error: Ar message .
.It 2
Usage error, or an output or system error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check a spec, then generate everything but the documentation into
.Pa obj :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cblink-gen -n kv.yaml
$ cblink-gen -m h,c,client,server -o obj kv.yaml
.Ed
.Pp
Write the tree diagram and the Markdown of a YANG module, with the SIDs
of its
.Pa .sid
file, into
.Pa ietf-ip.tree
and
.Pa ietf-ip.md :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cblink-gen -m md,tree -s ietf-ip@2018-02-22.sid \
    ietf-ip@2018-02-22.yang
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cblink 3 ,
.Xr capsicum 4
